safix::onepassword_signed_out

  × the 1Password command would not answer for the declared account
  │ 'fixture.example.com', so no side of any mapping
  │ was read and nothing was written.
  │ 
  │ The session is yours rather than safix's: safix never signs in, mints,
  │ holds
  │ or prints a session token, and it never puts one in an argument vector.
  │ What
  │ the child process inherits is whatever your own environment carries — a
  │ service-account token in OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN, or a session your own
  │ `op signin` established in this shell.
  │ 
  │ This refusal precedes the first read, which is why safix's own side of no
  │ mapping has been decrypted.
  │ 
  │ The command said:
  │ 
